**Copy Activity Advanced Concepts:**

**Source-Specific Optimizations:**
```
SQL Server Sources:
├─ partitionOption: Use column to split reads (improves parallelism)
├─ Example: SELECT * FROM table WHERE id BETWEEN @Incremental_partition_start_id AND @Incremental_partition_end_id
├─ Benefit: Parallel queries from same table
├─ Setup: Define partition column and range

Azure Blob Storage Sources:
├─ folderPath: Directory structure for organization
├─ Example: gs://bucket/year=2024/month=01/day=15/
├─ wildcard: Pattern matching for flexible paths
├─ Benefit: Only copy matching files
├─ Data Lake Hierarchy: Critical for performance

REST API Sources:
├─ requestMethod: GET/POST/PUT/DELETE
├─ requestBody: JSON payload for POST
├─ paginationRules: Handle multiple pages
├─ Benefit: Extract from web services
├─ Limitation: Usually slower than native connectors

Incremental Loading Sources:
├─ watermarkColumn: Track changes by timestamp
├─ watermarkValue: Store last processed value
├─ Example: WHERE ModifiedDate > '2024-01-01'
├─ Storage: Keep in metadata table
└─ Update: After successful load, update watermark
```

**Sink-Specific Optimizations:**
```
SQL Database Sinks:
├─ writeBatchSize: 5000-50000 (balance memory vs speed)
├─ writeBatchTimeout: How long to wait before flushing
├─ preCopyScript: Run before copy (truncate table, set identity)
├─ postCopyScript: Run after copy (index rebuilds, statistics)
├─ sqlWriterTableType: Use table type for bulk insert (faster)

Example Full Load Configuration:
