**Incremental Loading Deep Dive:**

**Watermark Implementation Pattern (Complete Example):**
```
Metadata Table Setup:
CREATE TABLE watermarks (
  TableName VARCHAR(100) PRIMARY KEY,
  LastLoadDate DATETIME DEFAULT '1900-01-01',
  LastLoadValue INT DEFAULT 0
);

Pipeline Configuration:
{
  "name": "IncrementalLoadPipeline",
  "properties": {
    "activities": [
      {
        "name": "GetWatermark",
        "type": "Lookup",
        "typeProperties": {
          "source": {
            "type": "SqlSource",
            "sqlReaderQuery": 
              "SELECT LastLoadDate FROM watermarks WHERE TableName='Customers'"
          },
          "dataset": {"referenceName": "MetadataDataset"},
          "firstRowOnly": true
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "CopyIncrementalData",
        "type": "Copy",
        "dependsOn": [{"activity": "GetWatermark", "dependencyConditions": ["Succeeded"]}],
        "typeProperties": {
          "source": {
            "type": "SqlSource",
            "sqlReaderQuery": 
              "@concat('SELECT * FROM Customers WHERE ModifiedDate > ''', 
                       activity('GetWatermark').output.firstRow.LastLoadDate, 
                       '''')
          },
          "sink": {
            "type": "ParquetSink",
            "storeSettings": {
              "path": "bronze/customers/@{utcnow('yyyy/MM/dd')}/data.parquet"
            }
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "UpdateWatermark",
        "type": "SqlServerStoredProcedure",
        "dependsOn": [{"activity": "CopyIncrementalData", "dependencyConditions": ["Succeeded"]}],
        "typeProperties": {
          "storedProcedureName": "sp_UpdateWatermark",
          "storedProcedureParameters": {
            "TableName": "Customers",
            "NewWatermarkDate": {"value": "@utcnow()", "type": "String"}
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}

Stored Procedure to Update Watermark:
CREATE PROCEDURE sp_UpdateWatermark
  @TableName NVARCHAR(100),
  @NewWatermarkDate DATETIME
AS
BEGIN
  UPDATE watermarks 
  SET LastLoadDate = @NewWatermarkDate 
  WHERE TableName = @TableName;
END;

Key Benefits:
├─ Only new/changed rows copied
├─ Reduces data movement costs
├─ Faster pipeline execution
├─ Can detect deletes with bit flag
└─ Scalable for many tables
```

**CDC (Change Data Capture) Pattern:**
```
SQL Server CDC Setup:
-- Enable CDC on database
EXEC sys.sp_cdc_enable_db;

-- Enable CDC on table
EXEC sys.sp_cdc_enable_table
  @source_schema = 'dbo',
  @source_name = 'Customers',
  @role_name = NULL;

Query Changes:
SELECT * FROM cdc.fn_cdc_get_all_changes_dbo_Customers
(@from_lsn, @to_lsn, N'all')

Returns:
├─ __$operation: 1=Delete, 2=Insert, 3=Update (before), 4=Update (after)
├─ __$seqval: Sequence for ordering
├─ __$update_mask: Which columns changed
└─ Original row data with changes

Pipeline Integration:
{
  "name": "CDCIncrementalLoad",
  "activities": [
    {
      "name": "GetLastLSN",
      "type": "Lookup",
      "typeProperties": {
        "source": {
          "sqlReaderQuery": 
            "SELECT max_lsn FROM cdc.lsn_time_mapping WHERE tbl_name='Customers'"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "ProcessChanges",
      "type": "Copy",
      "typeProperties": {
        "source": {
          "sqlReaderQuery": 
            "@concat('SELECT * FROM cdc.fn_cdc_get_all_changes_dbo_Customers(',
                     activity('GetLastLSN').output.firstRow.max_lsn,
                     ', CONVERT(BINARY(10), CONVERT(BIGINT, 9223372036854775807)), ''all'')')"
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}

Advantages over Timestamp Watermark:
├─ Detects deletes automatically
├─ Captures update order precisely
├─ Minimal overhead on source
├─ Works with non-monotonic timestamps
└─ Supports complex transformations
```

