## Integration Patterns

### Modern Data Warehouse Pattern (Medallion Architecture)

**Three-Tier Data Lake Implementation:**
```
Architecture Layers:

Raw Zone (Bronze):
├─ Purpose: Store source data in original form
├─ Format: Parquet (compressed, queryable)
├─ Partitioning: By date (@{formatDateTime(utcnow(), 'yyyy/MM/dd')})
├─ Retention: 6-12 months (cost optimization)
├─ Processing: Copy activity only (minimal transformation)
└─ Access: Read-only for data engineers

Refined Zone (Silver):
├─ Purpose: Cleansed, validated, business-rule data
├─ Format: Parquet (denormalized, optimized for joins)
├─ Partitioning: By date + entity (orders/customers/products)
├─ Quality: Deduplication, null handling, type validation
├─ Encryption: Column-level for sensitive data
├─ Processing: Data Flow for transformations
└─ Access: Business analysts can query directly

Analytics Zone (Gold):
├─ Purpose: Dimensional model ready for BI tools
├─ Format: Parquet + Synapse/SQL Database tables
├─ Structure: Dimensions + Facts (star schema)
├─ Aggregations: Pre-calculated metrics (date, region, product)
├─ Performance: Indexed for 100ms query latency
├─ Processing: Data Flow + SQL transformations
└─ Access: Power BI, reporting tools, direct queries
```

