**Q14: Troubleshooting: Pipeline runs slowly. What would you check?**

A: Systematic approach to performance debugging:

```
Performance Investigation Checklist:

1. Identify the Slow Activity
   └─ Check activity execution details
   └─ Look at actual vs baseline duration
   └─ Compare DIU/parallel copies settings

2. Common Causes & Solutions:

Source Bottleneck:
├─ Symptom: Source reads < 50 MB/sec
├─ Check: Run source query directly (is it slow?)
├─ Solution: Add indexes to source tables
├─ Solution: Filter at source (WHERE clause)
├─ Solution: Increase parallelCopies for multi-file sources
└─ Verification: Run source query, check execution plan

Network Bottleneck:
├─ Symptom: Slow even with small data
├─ Check: Network bandwidth utilization
├─ Check: Integration Runtime location (same region as source?)
├─ Solution: Move Self-Hosted IR closer to source
├─ Solution: Enable staging for compression
├─ Solution: Increase DIU allocation
└─ Verification: Monitor IR network metrics

Sink Bottleneck:
├─ Symptom: Copy activity takes long time
├─ Check: Sink database performance
├─ Check: Blocking queries, locks
├─ Solution: Increase writeBatchSize (100-50000)
├─ Solution: Enable staging + PolyBase
├─ Solution: Disable indexes during load
└─ Verification: Check sink database wait stats

Staging Performance:
├─ Symptom: Staging enables but no improvement
├─ Check: Staging storage location (same region?)
├─ Check: Storage account throughput limits
├─ Solution: Use different storage account for staging
├─ Solution: Use Premium tier (higher IOPS)
└─ Verification: Monitor staging blob metrics

3. Specific Troubleshooting:

Data Flow Slow:
├─ Issue: Data transformation slow
├─ Check: Partition distribution (skew?)
├─ Check: Join condition (many duplicates?)
├─ Check: Cluster size appropriate?
├─ Solution: Increase cluster size
├─ Solution: Pre-filter data
├─ Solution: Optimize join conditions
└─ Solution: Use caching for reused data

Lookup Activity Slow:
├─ Issue: Lookup returns > 100K rows
├─ Check: Lookup dataset size
├─ Solution: Add WHERE filter to lookup
├─ Solution: Cache result (if reused)
├─ Solution: Use Merge Join instead of Lookup
└─ Verification: Check Lookup output row count

Foreach Loop Slow:
├─ Issue: Loop with many iterations slow
├─ Check: Sequential vs parallel execution
├─ Check: Iterations count
├─ Solution: Enable parallel execution (batchCount=16)
├─ Solution: Consolidate iterations
└─ Verification: Monitor ForEach metrics

4. Metrics to Monitor:

For Copy Activity:
├─ rowsCopied / duration = throughput
├─ dataRead vs dataWritten (should match)
├─ failedRowCount (data quality issues)
├─ Example: 10 GB in 100 sec = 100 MB/sec

For Data Flow:
├─ executionDuration (total time)
├─ rowsRead vs rowsWritten (filter effectiveness)
├─ partitionCount (skew detection)
└─ Example: 1M rows in 30 sec = acceptable

For Pipeline:
├─ Critical path (longest dependency chain)
├─ Activity duration trend (increasing = degradation)
├─ Cost per activity (ROI on optimization)
└─ Example: 30 min pipeline should complete < 25 min

5. Resolution Process:

