**Q15: Cost Optimization: How would you reduce ADF costs by 50%?**

A: Multi-pronged cost reduction strategy:

```
Quick Wins (15-20% savings):

1. Reduce Execution Frequency
   ├─ Change hourly → daily (24x reduction)
   ├─ Batch small changes instead of real-time
   ├─ Only execute when needed (event-based trigger)
   └─ Impact: Biggest savings component

2. Reduce Data Movement
   ├─ Filter at source (no unnecessary columns)
   ├─ Select only needed columns
   ├─ Incremental loads (watermarks) vs full refresh
   └─ Example: 100GB → 10GB per run (90% savings)

3. Optimize DIU Allocation
   ├─ Current: DIU 32 for 100 MB data (over-provisioned)
   ├─ Change: DIU 4 (sufficient for 100 MB)
   ├─ Save: 8x cost reduction
   ├─ Test: Measure duration, SLA still met?
   └─ Implementation: Test in dev, gradually lower DIU

Moderate Effort (20-30% savings):

4. Enable Staging + Compression
   ├─ Staging + PolyBase: 10x faster (can lower DIU)
   ├─ Compression: 70% smaller transfers (less cost)
   ├─ Lower DIU from 32 → 8 (due to faster completion)
   ├─ Cost: Minimal (staging storage cheap)
   └─ Savings: 60% on copy activity costs

5. Consolidate Small Pipelines
   ├─ 10 pipelines @ 1 activity each → 1 pipeline @ 10 activities
   ├─ Execution count: 10 → 1 (90% reduction)
   ├─ Cost: Activity execution charges drop dramatically
   └─ Example: $50/month → $5/month

6. Use Incremental Loading
   ├─ Full refresh: 1 GB daily @ 50 activities = $500/month
   ├─ Incremental: 100 MB daily (changed only) = $50/month
   ├─ Watermark implementation (1 lookup + filter)
   ├─ Implementation effort: 4 hours
   └─ Savings: 90% with proper design

Advanced Optimization (30-50% savings):

7. Implement Data Lake Tiering
   ├─ Hot: Recent data (fast, high-cost)
   ├─ Warm: 3-month data (slower, medium-cost)
   ├─ Cold: Archive (very slow, cheapest)
   ├─ Move old data automatically (lifecycle policy)
   └─ Storage savings: 40-60%

8. Schedule Off-Peak Execution
   ├─ Run during off-peak hours (lower region costs)
   ├─ Example: US East (cheaper) vs US West (expensive)
   ├─ Reserved capacity (30% discount)
   ├─ Spot pricing where available
   └─ Savings: 20-30%

9. Decommission Unused Resources
   ├─ Audit all pipelines (many unused?)
   ├─ Delete development pipelines in production
   ├─ Consolidate similar pipelines
   ├─ Remove debug/test activities
   └─ Example: Savings varies

10. Implement Data Flow Caching
    ├─ Reused lookup tables only computed once
    ├─ Share results across activities
    ├─ Lower cluster utilization
    ├─ Reduced Data Flow time
    └─ Savings: 20-40% for data flow heavy pipelines

Cost Optimization Roadmap:

Month 1 (Quick Wins):
├─ Audit execution frequency
├─ Change from hourly → daily (biggest impact)
├─ Reduce unnecessary columns (SELECT * → SELECT columns)
├─ Estimated savings: 30-40%

